=== /tmp/u/tools/mesa/air-frontend.patch
ok
The text leading up to this was:
--------------------------
|Teach ir3_compiler to read AIR, the way it already reads SPIR-V.
|
|ir3_cmdline.c takes GLSL, TGSI and SPIR-V and compiles each for an Adreno. A
|.metallib (or one module's bitcode) is one more front end to it, and putting it
|here rather than in a tool of our own means the AIR path is compiled by the same
|ir3 the port's Mesa uses, with the same options, and that a regression in ir3
|shows against AIR as it does against the others.
|
|--chip-id takes the Adreno's chip id instead of the old gpu-id, because the
|the POCO X5 Pro's Adreno 7c+ Gen 3 (A635) has no gpu-id of its own: freedreno knows it
|only as chip_id 0x007506030500.
|
|It also declares air_run here, next to ir3_compiler: air_run draws with a translated shader and
|reads the pixel back, and it needs libgallium, which meson has not defined yet where the rest of
|the frontend is read (src/compiler comes before src/gallium). Its source stays with the frontend.
|
|Also removes this tool's own call of ir3_nir_lower_variant, which is a bug of
|the tool: ir3_context_init already calls it on its clone of the NIR, and the
|const-state setup inside asserts the second time. It shows on any shader whose
|const state reserves something -- every vertex shader, and anything with image
|dimensions -- and hides on the rest, which is presumably why it survived.
|--- a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/ir3/ir3_cmdline.c
|+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/ir3/ir3_cmdline.c
--------------------------
